OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786148289
OL,3,CTemperatures expected to reach 36C as
OL,4,Cheatwave conditions return to UK
OL,6,FParts of the UK could reach 36C next
OL,7,Fweek, with heat health alerts in place
OL,8,Fwarning that the hot weather is likely
OL,9,Fto affect the wellbeing of the
OL,10,Fpopulation.
OL,12,FThe Met Office said temperatures will
OL,13,Fclimb through the weekend.
OL,15,FThis summer has already seen two
OL,16,Frecord-breaking heatwaves, in May and
OL,17,FJune, that led to more than 2,800
OL,18,Fexcess deaths, and two more heatwaves
OL,19,Fin July that have fuelled drought and
OL,20,Fwildfires.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G1/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31302
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786148289
OL,3,CTemperatures expected to reach 36C as
OL,4,Cheatwave conditions return to UK
OL,6,FThe highest temperature of the year
OL,7,Fwas 38C recorded at Lingwood in
OL,8,FNorfolk on June 28.
OL,10,FThere have been 33 days so far this
OL,11,Fyear when temperatures have exceeded
OL,12,F30C somewhere in the UK.
OL,14,FThe record is 34 days in 1995, so that
OL,15,Frecord is likely to be broken next
OL,16,Fweek.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31303
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786148289
OL,3,CTemperatures expected to reach 36C as
OL,4,Cheatwave conditions return to UK
OL,6,FForecasters said the weekend will see
OL,7,Fa north-south split in the weather
OL,8,Fwith Scotland and Northern Ireland
OL,9,Flikely to see spells of heavy rain,
OL,10,Fwhile England and Wales will remain
OL,11,Flargely dry, sunny and increasingly
OL,12,Fwarm.
OL,14,FTemperatures could reach 27C on Friday
OL,15,Fand as high as 30C on Saturday, before
OL,16,Fclimbing into the low 30s in southern
OL,17,Fand south-east England on Sunday.
OL,19,FHighs of up to 30C are possible across
OL,20,Fparts of England and Wales on Tuesday,
OL,21,Fincreasing to 32C to 34C on Wednesday.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31304
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786148289
OL,3,CTemperatures expected to reach 36C as
OL,4,Cheatwave conditions return to UK
OL,6,FThe highest temperatures are currently
OL,7,Fexpected on Thursday when 36C could be
OL,8,Fseen in parts of East Anglia and south-
OL,9,Feast England.
OL,11,FDeputy chief forecaster Mike
OL,12,FSilverstone said: "Temperatures will
OL,13,Fclimb through the weekend and, more
OL,14,Fsignificantly, through much of next
OL,15,Fweek.
OL,17,F"After a brief dip on Monday, high
OL,18,Fpressure will move across the UK
OL,19,Fbefore settling to the east, allowing
OL,20,Fa southerly flow to develop.
OL,26,@tD@SOUyD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31305
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786148289
OL,3,CTemperatures expected to reach 36C as
OL,4,Cheatwave conditions return to UK
OL,6,F"A fairly widespread heatwave is
OL,7,Flikely across large parts of England
OL,8,Fand Wales, with hot conditions
OL,9,Fdeveloping in places.
OL,11,F"The heat is expected to peak for much
OL,12,Fof England, Wales, Northern Ireland
OL,13,Fand Scotland on Wednesday, with up to
OL,14,F34C possible in parts of central and
OL,15,Fsouthern England and south-east Wales.
OL,17,F"East Anglia and south-east England,
OL,18,Fhowever, could see temperatures even
OL,19,Fhigher on Thursday.
OL,26,@nD@AOUsD@AOUyD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31306
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786148289
OL,3,CTemperatures expected to reach 36C as
OL,4,Cheatwave conditions return to UK
OL,6,F"Humidity levels are also expected to
OL,7,Fincrease through the week, which may
OL,8,Fmake conditions feel more
OL,9,Funcomfortable, particularly overnight."
OL,11,FThe UK Health Security Agency (UKHSA)
OL,12,Fhas issued yellow heat health alerts
OL,13,Ffor the East Midlands, West Midlands,
OL,14,FSouth East, South West, East of
OL,15,FEngland, Yorkshire and the Humber, and
OL,16,FLondon.
OL,18,FThey will come into force at 9am on
OL,19,FSaturday and end at 9pm on Tuesday.
OL,26,@nD@AOUqD@gO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/12
